> Are they not supposed to be hostile until I come back up with the Amulet?

Neither Asmodeus nor Baalzebub will bother you until they come face to
face with you or their HP are somehow reduced (by a bouncing wand
attack, pet, etc.)  If Excalibur is not an issue (either then, or when
you entered the level), and you don't have the amulet, they are
generated peaceful.  If you have gold, they will ask you for a bribe. 
If you pay, they vanish laughing about foolish mortals.  If not, they
turn on you.

If you are wielding or carrying Excalibur, or have the amulet when you
arrive on their level, they will be generated hostile, but will still
not move until you come into their line of sight.

As for Juiblex, he has speed 3 (IIRC, 12 is normal), so he moves VERY
slowly.  He also waits for you to show up, but since his level is
completely open, he is more likely to wake up and come find you.  He
is not a bribable monster, but he is one that can be summoned by
same-race summoning.  If you are chaotic, summoned demons are
peaceful, so one way around him as a chaotic is to sacrifice your own
race until he shows up, then leave him alone.  A wizard mode test
shows that possessing the amulet of yendor did not change this
behaviour.

